.TH X-SIDECHAIN 1 "2026-09-19" "x-sidechain 0.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
x\-sidechain \- provider\-agnostic, evidence\-first multi\-agent deliberation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B x\-sidechain
.I COMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B x\-sidechain
runs a chaired deliberation between agents hosted by different providers.
Each agent works in a private workspace, publishes a bounded public brief,
answers the chair's clarifications, and reviews the chair's draft. Every
public event is written to a hash\-chained audit log.
.PP
A session is bounded before it starts: one full cycle costs at most
3N + min(Q, N) + 2 model calls, for N agents and Q clarification questions.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run \-\-config \fIFILE.json\fR \-\-prompt \fITEXT\fR
Run every configured agent on a task and print the final result.
Add
.B \-\-interactive
to send a correction to the room while the agents work.
.TP
.B ui " [" \-\-config \fIFILE.json\fR "] [" \-\-port \fIPORT\fR "] [" \-\-no\-browser ]
Serve the local interface on the loopback address and open it. Without
.BR \-\-config ,
the file named under
.B FILES
is used when it exists.
.TP
.B validate\-config \-\-config \fIFILE.json\fR
Check a configuration without making any provider call.
.TP
.B providers \-\-config \fIFILE.json\fR
List the configured providers.
.TP
.B auth login \fIPROVIDER\fR \-\-config \fIFILE.json\fR
Authenticate a provider through its own official flow.
.TP
.B auth status \fIPROVIDER\fR \-\-config \fIFILE.json\fR
Report whether a provider is authenticated.
.TP
.B verify \fIAUDIT.jsonl\fR
Verify that an audit log's hash chain is intact.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/x\-sidechain/config.json
Configuration loaded by
.B ui
when no
.B \-\-config
is given. Honours
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME .
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/x\-sidechain/sessions/
Audit logs and private agent workspaces, created owner\-only.
.SH SECURITY
The interface binds the loopback address only, requires a one\-off token, and
refuses a request whose Host or Origin is not its own address. A provider
secret's value never reaches the interface: it is told the variable's name and
whether it is set. Provider error text is scrubbed of credentials before it is
stored.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command completed.
.TP
.B 1
The command failed; the reason is printed to standard error.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project documentation: \fIhttps://github.com/gsmarcil/X\-SIDECHAIN\fR
